# OverviewService: a second @remote layer on top of CatalogService.

@server = http://localhost:5005/odata/v4/overview
@alice = Basic alice:alice
@bob = Basic bob:bob


### Renamed again (CustomerName -> Name); the exists flags read Contacts once for all rows of the answer
GET {{server}}/Customers?$select=ID,Name,RegionManager,HasContacts,HasAccounting&$top=4
Authorization: {{alice}}

### A filter on an exists flag is answered by a semi-join. The key set was read at start (@remote.warmUp): the log of
### the consumer shows no request to Contacts for it
GET {{server}}/Customers?$filter=HasAccounting eq true&$select=ID,Name
Authorization: {{alice}}

### $search through two layers: GroupName is a path column of the layer below, which plans the push-down
GET {{server}}/Customers?$search=retail&$select=ID,Name,GroupName
Authorization: {{alice}}

### A layer with a flag of its own that is not searched, the same searched columns as below: $search, $top and $count go down together
GET {{server}}/CustomerFinder?$search=a&$top=2&$count=true&$select=ID,CustomerName,HasContacts
Authorization: {{alice}}

### The next page of the same search
GET {{server}}/CustomerFinder?$search=a&$top=2&$skip=2&$count=true&$select=ID,CustomerName,HasContacts
Authorization: {{alice}}

### $search on an OData V2 source is case-sensitive (CatalogService/Products?$search=DESK finds nothing). ProductFinder
### keeps a search copy (@remote.warmUp search: 'read'): DESK finds "Standing Desk", ignoring case
GET {{server}}/ProductFinder?$search=DESK&$count=true&$select=ID,Name,CategoryName
Authorization: {{alice}}

### $filter, $orderby, the page and $count are applied to the copy (no request to producer-products)
GET {{server}}/ProductFinder?$search=E&$filter=Price lt 100&$orderby=Price desc&$top=2&$count=true&$select=ID,Name,Price
Authorization: {{alice}}

### A count only on the copy
GET {{server}}/ProductFinder?$search=MOUSE&$top=0&$count=true
Authorization: {{alice}}

### search: 'push' with where (Blocked = false): a $filter with Blocked eq false is answered from the copy, ignoring case.
### An unbound operation through the adapter (CatalogService setCustomerStatus) drops every cache: until the next
### warm-up run (about two minutes) this request goes to the backend, case-sensitive
GET {{server}}/AvailableProducts?$search=NOTEBOOK&$filter=Blocked eq false&$count=true&$select=ID,Name
Authorization: {{alice}}

### Without that filter the copy does not hold every row: the backend searches, case-sensitively (no product has "NOTEBOOK")
GET {{server}}/AvailableProducts?$search=NOTEBOOK&$count=true&$select=ID,Name
Authorization: {{alice}}

### exists over an association with a constant in its ON condition, with an infix filter, and through two hops
### (Items -> Products of producer-products)
GET {{server}}/OrderFlags?$select=ID,HasActiveItems,HasLargeItems,HasBlockedProduct
Authorization: {{alice}}

### The projection's WHERE: Status = 'O' pushed, _Customer.ValidTo >= $now evaluated in memory
GET {{server}}/OpenOrders?$select=ID,CustomerName,CustomerValidTo
Authorization: {{alice}}

### A read by key re-checks the WHERE: O002 is closed, so 404
GET {{server}}/OpenOrders('O002')
Authorization: {{alice}}

### $user in the WHERE: bob sees the orders bob created
GET {{server}}/MyOrders
Authorization: {{bob}}

### ...and alice hers
GET {{server}}/MyOrders
Authorization: {{alice}}

### GROUP BY with HAVING count(ID) > 1
GET {{server}}/BusyCustomers
Authorization: {{alice}}

### GROUP BY on two columns. X-Cache: HIT already the first time: @remote.warmUp read it when the server started
GET {{server}}/SalesByStatus?$filter=Status eq 'O'
Authorization: {{alice}}

### Another page and order of the same filter shares the cached entry: X-Cache: HIT
GET {{server}}/SalesByStatus?$filter=Status eq 'O'&$orderby=Total desc&$top=1
Authorization: {{alice}}

### DISTINCT
GET {{server}}/Currencies
Authorization: {{alice}}


### -------------------------------------------------------------- Entries: writes through a second layer
### CDS copied @remote.write.asInsert / @remote.write.operation from OrderManagementService.Entries; the layer below
### converts each write once. CREATE: one POST with Op = 'C'
POST {{server}}/Entries
Authorization: {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "CompanyCode": "1000", "DocNo": "100004", "Note": "Accrual November" }

### UPDATE: sent down as UPDATE, posted to the backend with Op = 'U'
PATCH {{server}}/Entries(CompanyCode='1000',DocNo='100004')
Authorization: {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "Note": "Accrual November, corrected" }

### DELETE: sent down as DELETE, posted to the backend with Op = 'D'
DELETE {{server}}/Entries(CompanyCode='1000',DocNo='100004')
Authorization: {{alice}}

### 404: deleted
GET {{server}}/Entries(CompanyCode='1000',DocNo='100004')
Authorization: {{alice}}
